$ perfwatch bogus
exit: 2
--- stdout
--- stderr
perfwatch: unknown command "bogus"

Usage: perfwatch <command> [flags]

Commands:
  run        sample CPU and RAM every second until interrupted
  top        rank the programs that used the most CPU and RAM
  peaks      list the peak episodes and who caused them
  actions    list a coding agent's tool calls with the CPU and RAM each used
  hook       record one tool call from a Claude Code hook on stdin
  serve      serve the dashboard on 127.0.0.1
  export     write the dashboard of a range to one HTML file
  install    start the collector now and at every logon
  uninstall  stop the collector and its autostart; keep the data
  version    print the perfwatch version

Run "perfwatch <command> -h" for the flags of a command.
